# Me.md — User Profile Template
# Copy this file to ~/.xochitl/Me.md and fill it in.
# Target: 50-80 lines. Update "What I'm building" as your focus shifts.
# Everything else changes maybe once or twice a year.

## Who I am
[Your name]. [Role/occupation]. [One defining trait — how you move through the world.]

## My domains
- **[Domain 1]** — [what you're doing in it / what level you're at]
- **[Domain 2]** — [same]
- **[Domain 3]** — [same]

## How I think
- I tend to [e.g. start with big picture and work down / build from first principles up]
- I get stuck when [e.g. options are too open-ended]
- I make better decisions when [e.g. I've written the problem out first]
- I learn best by [e.g. connecting to things I already know]

## How I work
- Tools I live in: [list]
- My note-taking approach: [e.g. Zettelkasten, PARA, freeform]
- I prefer communication that is [e.g. direct, short, practical]
- Don't [e.g. give me three options when one recommendation is possible]

## What I'm building
- [Project/goal 1] — [one line on why it matters]
- [Project/goal 2] — [same]

## How I want you to work with me
- When I'm thinking out loud, [e.g. help me sharpen the idea, don't just agree]
- When I ask for options, [e.g. give me your recommendation first]
- I care about [e.g. accuracy, traceability, ideas that last]
- I don't need [e.g. summaries of what you just did, empty praise]
